It definitely does, Even when it's a little boy looking out a window.

125
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:10,000
So I'll tell you what. just tell me the story.

126
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:22,000
Early one Saturday morning in October here in Glen Allen, Virginia, my first grader called me over to a window and asked what those boys were doing outside.

127
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:27,000
I looked and saw a bunch of blue uniforms running around with grocery bags,

128
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:31,000
Told them that they were Cub Scouts collecting food for people who didn't have any.

129
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:36,000
He looked back out the window and turned to me and asked: Dad, can I be a Cub Scout?

130
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:41,000
Being a busy dad? that really wasn't something I had considered

131
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:46,000
And the first thing I thought of saying was: we'll see, which of course means no.

132
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:51,000
But for some reason I asked him: why do you want to be a Cub Scout?

133
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:55,000
He looked back out the window and thought a long time for a first grader,

134
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,000
And I could see the little gears turning in his head.

135
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:04,000
He turned back to me and looked me straight in the eye and said: Dad, Mom has been teaching me about character.

136
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:09,000
I want to be a boy with character and I want friends with character.

137
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:11,000
Those boys have character.

138
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:20,000
Dad, can I be a Cub Scout?

139
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,000
Well, we joined the next week.

140
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:27,000
He has lots of friends who both are characters and have characters.

141
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:33,000
He is a 13-year-old life scout now who's goal is to go to the Jamboree next year as an Eagle Scout.

142
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
What a touching story. What a great story.

143
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:39,000
